\section{The format}{

One row per taxon per survey. \code{unit} is the thing with the latent state (a
site, camera, pond, transect, or an individual animal), \code{taxon} a short
species code resolved in the \verb{__taxa} side table, \code{y} the observation.
\code{period} and \code{occasion} are the primary and secondary survey indices;
covariates are prefixed by the level at which they are constant (\code{unit_},
\code{period_}, \code{obs_}, \code{taxon_}). A row exists iff a survey happened: \code{y = 0} is
surveyed and not detected, a missing row is not surveyed, \code{y} is never \code{NA}.
}

